    "category": "Non-automatic weighing instrument",
    "type_designations": ["LP788"],
    "module_designation": "Not applicable",
    "description": "Self-indicating, single interval, non-automatic weighing instrument powered by rechargeable batteries, intended to be used as a portable instrument for weighing road vehicles. Shall not be used for direct sales to the public. Must be placed on flat, level ground such that the entire underside of the weighing area is supported, and the bubble level indicator within its limiting mark. Groups of associated LP788 instruments may be used for determining the total mass of a vehicle only if all wheels are supported simultaneously. Steel construction; integral LCD display; 4 operator push buttons; solar panel; 66 cm x 39 cm load receptor with grip tape surface; level indicator (indicates 3° tilt limit); fixed steel handle. Sealing: access to the electronics, load cell and calibration jumper is prevented by sealing the enclosure using a wire and seal method. There are currently no authorised alternatives."
